-- Accept natural filing targets and guide callbacks through date, period, clock and confirmed timezone.
UPDATE daisy_call_scripts SET history=coalesce(history,'[]'::jsonb)||jsonb_build_array(jsonb_build_object('version',version,'title',title,'category',category,'direction',direction,'content',content,'saved_at',now())),content=content||jsonb_build_object('script_text',replace(content->>'script_text','What day and time should we call you back, and what time zone is that?','What day would work best for your callback?'),'key_points',coalesce(content->'key_points','[]'::jsonb)||$rules$["Accept natural filing timelines such as I probably could file in a couple weeks, maybe a couple weeks, two days or a few months. Preserve the exact statement as a client-reported filing target and move on to arranging the callback. Never repeat the filing-time question just because the client used a plural unit.","For callbacks, offer computed date choices first. After choosing a date, ask whether morning or evening works better, then suggest 8 AM or 9 AM for morning or 6 PM or 7 PM for evening and accept another client-selected time. Preserve details already supplied. A bare hour such as 7 Eastern is ambiguous until the client chooses morning/evening or AM/PM. Do not assume PM. If they say 8 or 9, ask which one rather than silently choosing.","Use the saved ZIP to suggest a named timezone when a local lookup is available, then ask Is that correct? A ZIP timezone is a suggestion, never consent. Respect the client’s correction. If no reliable ZIP lookup is available, ask for their timezone. Read back the chosen date, exact time with AM/PM, and timezone once, and save through the existing callback scheduler only after the client agrees."]$rules$::jsonb),version=version+1,updated_at=now() WHERE script_number=40 AND version=32 AND deleted_at IS NULL;
